<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/porch-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/porch-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/porch-home.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="681" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Questions answered</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Answers by topic</p><h1>Mississippi Insurance Appraisal Questions, Answered</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers about how appraisal works, what it costs, deadlines, the Coast’s wind-and-flood questions and working with us.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="FAQ topics"><p class="glance-h">Jump to a topic</p><ul><li><a href="#faq-1">Appraisal basics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Costs &amp; fees</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Timing &amp; deadlines</a></li><li><a href="#faq-4">Coast, wind &amp; flood</a></li><li><a href="#faq-5">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="faq-1">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?</summary><p>Appraisal is a process written into most property policies for resolving a disagreement over the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the two pick an umpire, and agreement of any two sets the amount.</p></details><details><summary>Does appraisal decide whether my damage is covered?</summary><p>No. Appraisal values the loss; it generally does not decide coverage, causation disputes that turn on policy wording, or bad faith. Those questions stay with you, your carrier and, if needed, a Mississippi attorney and the courts.</p></details><details><summary>Is there a special Mississippi appraisal law?</summary><p>Appraisal in Mississippi comes from the appraisal clause in your policy rather than a dedicated state appraisal statute. That is why the exact deadlines and steps depend on your policy’s wording.</p></details><details><summary>When does appraisal make sense?</summary><p>It tends to fit when your carrier has accepted the claim but you disagree on scope or price, such as roof quantities, matching or unit costs. If the claim was denied outright, a coverage review with an attorney usually comes first.</p></details><details><summary>Can I start appraisal if I already cashed a partial payment?</summary><p>Usually yes. Cashing an undisputed payment typically doesn’t waive your right to dispute the rest, but read any release language carefully and confirm with a Mississippi attorney if a check came with conditions.</p></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Costs &amp; fees</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Who pays for appraisal?</summary><p>Under most clauses each side pays its own appraiser, and the umpire’s fee is usually split evenly. Your policy wording controls, so check the appraisal section.</p></details><details><summary>How do you charge?</summary><p>We quote fees in writing before we start, based on the size and complexity of the file. You will know the fee structure and what it covers before you sign anything.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to pay anything to ask a question?</summary><p>No. You can call or send us your carrier’s estimate and a short description of the dispute, and we’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal looks like a fit.</p></details><details><summary>Is appraisal cheaper than a lawsuit?</summary><p>Appraisal is often faster and less expensive than litigation because it focuses on one question: the amount of loss. It isn’t free, though, and it can’t award damages for bad faith or delay.</p></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Timing &amp; deadlines</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>How long do I have to name an appraiser?</summary><p>Many policies give each side 20 days after the written demand, but some forms use different windows. Read your appraisal clause and mark the date.</p></details><details><summary>How long do I have to file a lawsuit in Mississippi?</summary><p>Mississippi’s general limitation period for many contract claims is three years, and state law generally limits contracts from shortening statutory periods. Your situation may differ, so confirm your deadline with a Mississippi attorney.</p></details><details><summary>Does demanding appraisal pause my deadlines?</summary><p>Don’t assume it does. Policy deadlines and legal limitation periods may keep running during appraisal, so track them separately and ask a Mississippi attorney if you are close to one.</p></details><details><summary>How long do I have to collect recoverable depreciation?</summary><p>Many replacement cost policies require repairs to be completed within a set period, often stated in the loss settlement section. Check your policy and ask your carrier in writing if the period can be extended.</p></details><details><summary>Should I wait until repairs are done to start appraisal?</summary><p>Not necessarily. Many owners appraise before repairs so the amount is settled first, but you should still make reasonable temporary repairs to prevent further damage and keep the receipts.</p></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Coast, wind &amp; flood</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What is MWUA?</summary><p>The Mississippi Windstorm Underwriting Association is a residual-market insurer of wind and hail coverage for property in Hancock, Harrison, Jackson, Pearl River, Stone and George counties. Many coastal owners carry a homeowners policy that excludes wind plus a separate MWUA wind policy.</p></details><details><summary>Can appraisal split wind damage from flood damage?</summary><p>Appraisal can often put a value on the wind portion of a loss under a wind policy, but it generally cannot decide which cause is covered when the policy wording is in dispute. That question may need a Mississippi attorney.</p></details><details><summary>Why is my hurricane deductible so large?</summary><p>Many coastal policies use a percentage named-storm or wind deductible, often 2% to 5% of the Coverage A dwelling limit, instead of a flat dollar amount. Your declarations page shows the percentage and when it applies.</p></details><details><summary>Is flood covered by my homeowners policy?</summary><p>Usually not. Flood is typically covered by a separate policy, most often through the National Flood Insurance Program, which has its own claim and dispute rules.</p></details></div><h2 id="faq-5">Working with us</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Are you a law firm or a public adjuster?</summary><p>Neither. We are an independent appraisal practice. We don’t give legal advice, and we don’t adjust claims for a percentage; when legal questions come up, we’ll suggest you speak with a Mississippi attorney.</p></details><details><summary>Where in Mississippi do you work?</summary><p>We serve property owners across all 82 counties, from the Coast and the Pine Belt to the Delta, Metro Jackson and North Mississippi.</p></details><details><summary>What should I send you first?</summary><p>Your carrier’s estimate, the declarations page, any denial or payment letters, and your photos are the most useful starting points. A contractor estimate helps if you have one.</p></details><details><summary>Can I file a complaint with the state about my carrier?</summary><p>Yes. The Mississippi Insurance Department accepts consumer complaints about insurers. A complaint is separate from appraisal and doesn’t set the amount of loss, but it can create a record of delays or unanswered requests.</p></details><details><summary>Will you work with my contractor?</summary><p>Yes. Contractors often know the property best, and their measurements, photos and invoices can help support the scope. We keep our role as an appraiser separate from the repair contract.</p></details></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>Free first conversation. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> +1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-gold btn-block" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm CT</small></div><div class="side-box"><h2 class="side-h">Resources</h2><ul class="side-links"><li><a href="/appraisal-roadmap/">Appraisal roadmap</a></li><li><a href="/questions-answered/" aria-current="page">Questions answered</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-claim-terms/">Insurance claim terms</a></li><li><a href="/claim-advice/">Claim advice</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="band"><div class="wrap band-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email — we’re glad to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
